{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "id": "return-window-fees",
  "title": "Return windows and restocking fees",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "9c8cc9ec-5f65-4f05-8c60-c6ed5c8e72de",
      "question": "What return window and restocking fee apply to electronics and to furniture under Lumen's return policy, and are defective items charged the fee?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-03T04:13:53.963515Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-03T04:13:59.370757Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "Based on Lumen's Return and Refund Policy, here are the return windows and restocking fees for electronics and furniture:\n\n| Category | Return Window | Restocking Fee (Opened/Used, Not Defective) | Defective/Damaged Items |\n|----------|---------------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------------|\n| **Electronics** | 30 days | 15% | **No fee** |\n| **Furniture** | 45 days | 20% | **No fee; free pickup** |\n\n**Defective items are never charged a restocking fee** for either category. The policy explicitly states: \"Fees are charged only on items returned opened or used and never on defective or damaged items\" [1].\n\nAdditional notes:\n- The return window runs from the purchase date (in store) or delivery date (online/delivered orders)\n- Lumen Rewards Gold members receive 15 extra days on every window\n- Electronics also require serial number capture at return\n- For furniture returned by mail, defective items qualify for free pickup, while non-defective furniture incurs a $79 carrier pickup fee [1].\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Unstructured Retrieval evidence — 3 documents — evidence `hermes-receipt:6eb5551459aaa953894ab8b8c223f19d1875ef54d4fc0dbec58567cfa91fa3d0`",
        "citations": [
