                "chunkId": "retail.policies:f-17e1fb4d753ce9d2:0009",
                "title": "store-operations-sop.pdf",
                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Store Operations Standard Operating\nProcedures\n6. Returns and exchanges at the point of sale\n6.1 Processing steps\n- Greet the customer and ask for the receipt, the order number or the Lumen Rewards ID.\n- Look the order up in the point-of-sale system. If the item was bought online, scan the return barcode from the confirmation email or look up by order number.\n- Check the item against the category window in the policy. Gold members have 15 extra days.\n- Inspect the item and its packaging and record the condition code (table below).\n- For Electronics, scan the serial number into the return screen. A return of an Electronics item without a serial number needs Store Manager approval.\n- The system calculates the restocking fee from the category and condition. The cashier may not change it; only a Store Manager can apply the RF-WAIVE code.\n- Refund to the original payment method, or issue store credit where the rules require it. Print the receipt and have the customer sign for refunds above $100.00.\n- Place the item in the returns bin with its return tag. Returns are inspected and re-shelved or sent to the returns center within 24 hours.\nCND-U, Meaning = Unopened or unused. CND-U, Restocking fee = Never. CND-O, Meaning = Opened or used, not defective. CND-O, Restocking fee = Per policy category table. CND-D, Meaning = Defective or damaged. CND-D, Restocking fee = Never. RSN-01, Meaning = Changed mind or did not fit the space. RSN-01, Restocking fee = Per condition. RSN-02, Meaning ",
