                "title": "supplier-terms.docx",
                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Master Supplier Terms Summary, Fiscal 2026\n4. Returns to vendor and defect allowances\n- **Defect allowance.** Each supplier credits Lumen automatically, every quarter, a percentage of the net cost of units sold equal to its defect allowance in the table above. The allowance covers units returned by customers as defective or damaged.\n- **Returns to vendor (RTV).** Defective units above the allowance are returned to the supplier for full credit of the invoiced cost, plus freight. The supplier must issue a return authorization within 5 business days and credit within 30 days of receipt.\n- **Customer returns of opened items** that are not defective are Lumen's cost. They are recovered through the customer restocking fee in the Return and Refund Policy (POL-RET-014), not from the supplier.\n- **Clusters.** If defective returns of one item exceed 6 percent of units sold in a rolling 60 days, the supplier must open a quality investigation and may be asked to fund a stock withdrawal.",
